WEBVTT

00:03.020 --> 00:06.250
The duet project is finally starting.

00:06.250 --> 00:07.230
Yes.

00:07.230 --> 00:10.360
I wonder what your partner,
Otori Eiji-san, is like.

00:11.050 --> 00:13.700
I heard he's Otori Eiichi-san's
younger brother.

00:14.020 --> 00:15.650
No matter what he's like,

00:15.650 --> 00:20.470
as the first of the duet projects,
I plan to stay focused on our work.

00:36.840 --> 00:37.930
That's...

02:44.010 --> 02:46.030
That was wonderful, you two.

02:47.130 --> 02:48.670
Thank you.

02:48.670 --> 02:51.690
It's a great song, isn't it?

02:51.690 --> 02:56.480
Yeah. When I heard it performed onstage
in London, I fell in love with it instantly.

02:56.480 --> 02:58.440
What? You saw it in London?

02:58.810 --> 03:01.210
My brother dragged me
around to a lot of places.

03:01.210 --> 03:05.120
Really? I've seen it plenty of times on DVD,

03:05.120 --> 03:07.120
but I'd like to see it
performed in person someday.

03:08.170 --> 03:10.290
If I recall correctly, in that scene...

03:14.490 --> 03:15.880
They used this dance step, right?

03:15.880 --> 03:17.940
Yes, that's right.

03:19.160 --> 03:20.900
Are you familiar with this step?

03:20.900 --> 03:21.930
Of course.

03:27.180 --> 03:31.700
I'm so glad I get to dance with you, Ichinose-san.

03:31.700 --> 03:35.160
I think we'll have fun working
together on the duet project.

03:38.020 --> 03:39.690
I haven't introduced myself yet.

03:40.430 --> 03:41.810
I'm Otori Eiji.

03:42.400 --> 03:44.890
Thank you for today.

03:44.890 --> 03:47.070
We were just supposed to make introductions,

03:47.070 --> 03:48.720
but we even had time to discuss the song.

03:48.720 --> 03:49.650
It was no problem.

03:49.650 --> 03:54.240
We were able to settle on a concept,
and I enjoyed our conversation.

03:54.240 --> 03:55.460
So did I.

03:55.460 --> 04:00.610
I'll create a demo tape
based on the ideas you gave me.

04:00.610 --> 04:02.030
Thanks.

04:02.030 --> 04:03.340
Excuse me.

04:03.870 --> 04:08.100
I had fun singing that song with you today.

04:08.810 --> 04:10.640
I love that song.

04:11.790 --> 04:14.730
The only time I've really heard it, though, was when I saw it performed onstage.

04:14.730 --> 04:16.770
What? Only once?

04:16.770 --> 04:20.810
Yes, but after singing it together,

04:21.430 --> 04:26.290
I understand now why my father said
you're the greatest genius in STARISH.

04:27.640 --> 04:31.700
I'm not a genius.

04:33.500 --> 04:34.250
Excuse me.

04:35.410 --> 04:37.960
This is my phone number.

04:37.960 --> 04:42.170
Going forward, would you like
to come practice at our agency?

04:44.050 --> 04:46.970
But going to your studio...

04:47.410 --> 04:49.450
Is that a problem?

04:49.910 --> 04:53.460
We have a foreign choreographer
visiting right now,

04:53.460 --> 04:56.740
so I thought it would help
with the duet project.

05:01.000 --> 05:02.300
I'll think about it.

05:07.060 --> 05:09.150
Sorry I'm late.

05:11.090 --> 05:14.030
This is QUARTET NIGHT's tour?

05:14.030 --> 05:17.580
It's amazing that they'll be
performing at such huge venues.

05:18.170 --> 05:21.600
The fans are so excited, too.

05:21.600 --> 05:24.590
They're paying a lot of attention
to their dancing and production, too.

05:24.590 --> 05:28.470
It truly is an evolution to surpass a revolution, huh?

05:29.570 --> 05:32.680
I wish we could go on tour like QUARTET NIGHT.

05:33.150 --> 05:36.670
If we win the Triple S
decisive concert, we probably can.

05:36.670 --> 05:38.650
Yeah! I'm so excited.

05:39.510 --> 05:40.310
Tokiya.

05:40.730 --> 05:42.900
Welcome back. You're late.

05:42.900 --> 05:46.310
Sorry. The meeting ran late.

05:46.910 --> 05:47.820
Let's get start-

05:47.820 --> 05:50.990
What was he like?

05:50.990 --> 05:54.410
Is he unique like his brother?

05:57.770 --> 06:00.170
He's a genius.

06:01.080 --> 06:06.070
I sensed an overflowing talent
for singing and dancing from him.

06:06.070 --> 06:11.100
You don't usually offer such
high praise for people you've just met.

06:11.430 --> 06:15.750
People with talent
really are drawn to each other.

06:15.750 --> 06:18.560
I'm excited for the duet project, too.

06:19.580 --> 06:22.480
Guys, let's start practicing.

06:23.730 --> 06:25.280
Tokiya?

06:42.080 --> 06:45.220
Eiji, you were off during the same section again.

06:45.220 --> 06:46.690
Got it. Sorry.

06:46.690 --> 06:49.050
Let's try it again from the top.

06:49.470 --> 06:50.760
Yes, please.

06:50.760 --> 06:54.330
Beyond the gate (GO!) beyond eternity (GO!)

06:54.330 --> 06:57.720
The story that God doesn't even know

06:57.720 --> 07:04.770
We'll paint it the color of the HEAVENS

07:05.080 --> 07:06.360
Yes, call HEAVENS

07:06.810 --> 07:08.870
Yes, call HEAVENS

07:09.820 --> 07:11.550
Okay, let's take a break.

07:16.790 --> 07:18.510
What's he doing here?

07:30.180 --> 07:31.130
Ichinose-san.

07:32.280 --> 07:33.710
You invited him?

07:33.710 --> 07:37.180
Yeah, I invited him
so we could practice together.

07:38.150 --> 07:38.970
Should I not have?

07:41.300 --> 07:42.490
Do whatever you want.

07:44.250 --> 07:45.610
Ichinose-san.

07:45.930 --> 07:47.820
Sorry to keep you waiting.

07:47.820 --> 07:51.030
It's all right. I came too early.

07:51.030 --> 07:52.150
Sorry for the inconvenience.

07:52.150 --> 07:54.330
It's no trouble at all.

07:54.330 --> 07:58.060
I've been looking forward to today's practice.

08:13.420 --> 08:16.520
I'm glad I came today. I learned a lot.

08:16.520 --> 08:19.270
Really? I'm so glad.

08:24.120 --> 08:25.430
Well, well.

08:26.530 --> 08:30.230
Diving right into it, could you tell us
your impressions of working together?

08:30.730 --> 08:35.280
We're perfectly in sync during practice
like we've been working together forever.

08:35.280 --> 08:37.240
Every day is so much fun.

08:37.580 --> 08:39.230
Working with him is an experience

08:39.230 --> 08:42.830
more stimulating and enjoyable
than anything I've done before.

08:42.830 --> 08:45.280
I'm so glad to hear that.

08:45.280 --> 08:48.420
I wish we could sing together even more.

08:48.420 --> 08:50.420
That would be great.

09:06.750 --> 09:08.730
Is Ichinose Tokiya Leaving?!

09:06.750 --> 09:08.730
Ichinose Shows Great Enthusiasm for Group Project

09:06.750 --> 09:08.730
An Unexpected Shock?!

09:06.750 --> 09:08.730
Transfer to HEAVENS

09:11.610 --> 09:14.530
Hey, Tokiya. This article...

09:15.250 --> 09:17.070
That's yesterday's interview.

09:18.370 --> 09:20.200
Is Ichinose Tokiya Leaving?!

09:18.370 --> 09:20.200
Ichinose Shows Great Enthusiasm for Group Project

09:18.370 --> 09:20.200
An Unexpected Shock?!

09:18.370 --> 09:20.200
Transfer to HEAVENS

09:21.780 --> 09:22.790
What about it?

09:22.790 --> 09:27.460
What? Uh... Well, lately you've
been going to their studio a lot.

09:27.800 --> 09:30.420
It's to practice for the duet project.

09:30.420 --> 09:32.590
O-Of course.

09:32.930 --> 09:39.280
Don't you have more important things
to do than worry about this article?

09:39.280 --> 09:39.940
Huh?

09:39.940 --> 09:43.730
You were a little flat at the start again
on the music show the other day.

09:43.730 --> 09:44.310
What?

09:45.800 --> 09:46.850
Sorry...

09:58.050 --> 10:00.780
You two seem to be getting along.

10:02.790 --> 10:04.660
Raging Otori.

10:06.000 --> 10:07.470
Hello, sir.

10:08.410 --> 10:11.400
Thank you for letting me use your studio.

10:11.960 --> 10:13.590
It's been very stimulating.

10:13.590 --> 10:14.620
Excuse me.

10:16.910 --> 10:19.180
You're welcome to join us anytime.

10:21.070 --> 10:23.880
Did you tell them to write that article?

10:23.880 --> 10:27.730
You know I don't have that kind of power.

10:28.220 --> 10:32.230
But I do recognize your talent.

10:33.890 --> 10:35.130
Join us.

10:35.610 --> 10:37.860
You're good enough to make it internationally.

10:40.910 --> 10:44.090
I'll be doing that with STARISH.

10:44.090 --> 10:47.120
I see. With those members?

10:47.120 --> 10:49.410
That's quite the overly ambitious dream.

10:54.000 --> 10:55.180
Ichinose-san? Huh?

10:56.230 --> 10:57.210
Dad?

10:57.970 --> 11:01.640
If you ever want to do it, call me.

11:10.180 --> 11:12.610
What? Tokiya is transferring?

11:12.060 --> 11:13.900
Ichinose Tokiya to transfer from the Shining Agency to Raging Entertainment

11:12.060 --> 11:13.900
Preparing to transfer? Ichinose Tokiya seen coming and going daily from Raging's offices

11:12.610 --> 11:13.900
What is this?

11:14.270 --> 11:16.570
The articles are based entirely on speculation.

11:16.920 --> 11:18.900
Isn't he just going there to practice?

11:18.900 --> 11:22.240
Yeah. There's nothing fishy about it.

11:22.240 --> 11:26.370
Yeah. Tokiya-kun would never transfer agencies.

11:26.370 --> 11:31.960
People will say what they will,
but it's nothing for us to worry about.

11:34.310 --> 11:36.610
Hey. Welcome back, Icchi.

11:36.610 --> 11:39.590
Tokiya, more untrue articles came out.

11:41.510 --> 11:43.480
Don't worry about it.

11:44.300 --> 11:46.510
It's not funny.

11:53.320 --> 11:59.230
It's true that Raging Entertainment
is trying to recruit me.

12:01.260 --> 12:06.120
Raging Otori thinks highly of my abilities.

12:07.480 --> 12:09.330
He said I could make it internationally.

12:09.830 --> 12:10.620
What?

12:11.020 --> 12:12.330
What are you talking about?

12:13.370 --> 12:15.680
Tokiya-kun, did something happen?

12:15.680 --> 12:18.210
I have a goal.

12:19.180 --> 12:22.170
To go higher and further.

12:22.170 --> 12:23.810
What's gotten into you?

12:23.810 --> 12:26.800
I thought we were working towards
the decisive concert together!

12:27.780 --> 12:29.390
Let me be clear.

12:30.230 --> 12:35.320
At this rate, the gap between us,
QUARTET NIGHT and HEAVENS will only widen.

12:36.070 --> 12:38.660
I'm not satisfied with my current progress.

12:38.660 --> 12:42.650
I'm just trying to do what I have to do.

12:43.670 --> 12:48.030
If the rest of you remain stuck here...

12:53.160 --> 12:58.080
Then I plan to accept Raging Otori's invitation.

13:08.120 --> 13:09.250
Excuse me.

13:11.150 --> 13:12.380
Ichinose-san.

13:19.580 --> 13:20.340
Ichinose Tokiya Leaving STARISH

13:20.340 --> 13:22.230
Why now? What happened?

13:53.010 --> 13:56.470
Why don't we stop now
and pick this up tomorrow?

13:56.470 --> 13:57.100
Okay.

13:59.010 --> 14:02.070
Wow! Look at the time. I should—

14:02.070 --> 14:02.820
Excuse me!

14:04.390 --> 14:09.070
I'd like to keep practicing
today for as long as we can.

14:09.890 --> 14:11.530
Please stay with me.

14:16.060 --> 14:17.540
Sure.

14:17.540 --> 14:18.670
Okay.

14:21.620 --> 14:22.920
Thank you.

14:22.920 --> 14:26.210
Could we start from here, then?

14:26.850 --> 14:29.630
I'd also like to modify the lyrics here,
but what do you think?

14:29.630 --> 14:34.640
Also, I think we should turn this section
into a refrain, and during the chorus...

14:34.640 --> 14:38.590
Oh, I'm sorry. I'm just
offering all my own opinions.

14:39.140 --> 14:40.350
It's fine.

14:40.910 --> 14:42.650
Tell us more.

14:52.150 --> 14:55.870
We have to be work even harder.

14:56.630 --> 15:01.570
Icchi must have realized that after
he started working on the duet project.

15:03.310 --> 15:04.920
After starting as part of the first duo,

15:05.390 --> 15:07.710
he must have thought things
aren't good enough as they are.

15:08.530 --> 15:15.390
We didn't understand any of the
impatience and anxiety he was feeling.

15:16.530 --> 15:20.310
Tokiya-kun was fighting so desperately alone.

15:21.700 --> 15:25.520
We're the ones who made Tokiya say those things.

15:27.910 --> 15:30.990
We can't let it end like this.

15:43.290 --> 15:44.250
Ichinose-san.

15:45.620 --> 15:46.380
Nanami-san.

15:47.090 --> 15:47.710
It's finished.

15:50.520 --> 15:52.090
Thank you.

15:52.090 --> 15:56.720
I think they'll understand how you feel.

16:01.180 --> 16:05.650
I just wanted them to take this more seriously.

16:08.440 --> 16:12.320
So we can achieve what we're aiming for.

16:16.990 --> 16:17.700
Tokiya!

16:17.370 --> 16:18.200
Tokiya-kun!

16:17.700 --> 16:18.860
Ichinose!

16:18.200 --> 16:19.450
Tokiya!

16:35.970 --> 16:36.550
We—

16:43.790 --> 16:48.900
Before, I was happy as long
as I could sing, whether it was

16:48.900 --> 16:50.740
as HAYATO or Ichinose Tokiya.

16:52.020 --> 16:56.710
But after meeting you all,
becoming a member of STARISH,

16:56.710 --> 17:00.200
and singing onstage together numerous times...

17:02.780 --> 17:06.930
My desire to continue singing with
you all has become stronger than ever!

17:08.200 --> 17:11.460
Stronger than it ever was before!

17:14.140 --> 17:19.500
After meeting the amazing genius
that is Otori Eiji during the duet project

17:19.990 --> 17:25.290
and learning just how talented
HEAVENS is, honestly, I was shaken.

17:27.500 --> 17:29.900
I realized we couldn't continue as we were.

17:30.210 --> 17:37.110
We have to push ourselves
higher and further to keep up.

17:40.690 --> 17:41.910
Shinomiya-san.

17:43.170 --> 17:48.930
Your magnanimity and kindness
protect us like a shield.

17:50.970 --> 17:51.500
Syo.

17:52.200 --> 17:54.720
Your straightforwardness
and strength grant us

17:54.720 --> 17:59.380
the power to charge straight
through all obstacles.

18:01.110 --> 18:01.760
Ren.

18:02.730 --> 18:09.410
Your elegance and passion paint us
in brilliant colors and make us shine.

18:11.930 --> 18:13.130
Hijirikawa-san.

18:13.790 --> 18:21.800
Your calmness and steadfast
conviction always grant us courage.

18:22.980 --> 18:24.100
Aijima-san.

18:24.590 --> 18:28.310
Your love for music and the purity
of your emotions remind us

18:28.310 --> 18:33.210
of how we felt in the beginning
and grant us new awareness.

18:35.400 --> 18:36.300
Otoya.

18:36.990 --> 18:39.470
Your brilliant smile and voice are

18:39.470 --> 18:44.430
essential signposts that
inspire us and illuminate our future.

18:46.450 --> 18:51.570
QUARTET NIGHT and HEAVENS may
have some things we don't have...

18:52.210 --> 18:57.000
But we have plenty of potential
they don't have, either.

18:57.960 --> 19:02.870
I know the seven of us
can reach even greater heights.

19:05.530 --> 19:09.480
Let's continue heading towards
the future as STARISH...

19:12.520 --> 19:14.120
Together... As far as we can go.

19:25.060 --> 19:27.620
All right! Let's do it!

19:26.790 --> 19:28.100
We'll do our best.

19:34.290 --> 19:35.150
It's finished.

19:36.180 --> 19:36.690
Yes.

19:39.130 --> 19:42.740
When I think about how this is the end,
it makes me a little sad.

19:45.090 --> 19:47.740
But it's a great song.

19:48.460 --> 19:50.330
Thanks to you, Ichinose-san.

19:52.570 --> 19:57.710
When we first met, you called me a genius.

19:59.320 --> 20:01.720
But I'm not a genius.

20:03.150 --> 20:07.930
The other members of STARISH
have far more talent than I do.

20:09.670 --> 20:14.100
I want to keep singing with them.

20:14.470 --> 20:17.950
So I have to keep working hard.

20:20.330 --> 20:24.300
I joined HEAVENS because my
father and brother told me to.

20:25.020 --> 20:30.290
At first, I wondered if I should even be an idol.

20:31.450 --> 20:37.960
But after working with you,
singing became more fun for me.

20:38.900 --> 20:43.590
It inspired me to work harder
on my projects with HEAVENS.

20:47.430 --> 20:51.050
I'm really glad I got to work with you.

20:51.690 --> 20:53.130
Thank you.

20:54.980 --> 20:57.440
Will you sing with me again?

20:59.330 --> 21:00.690
Of course.

21:02.220 --> 21:04.550
As Ichinose Tokiya of STARISH.

21:03.270 --> 21:05.780
Mighty wish

21:05.780 --> 21:08.940
And I as Otori Eiji of HEAVENS.

21:07.530 --> 21:11.400
Mighty shine

21:15.960 --> 21:21.550
It begins here

21:20.130 --> 21:21.550
Mighty Aura

21:21.550 --> 21:24.630
Encounters always come
suddenly like evening showers

21:24.630 --> 21:25.860
Mighty Aura

21:25.860 --> 21:29.010
Your voice violates the airspace of my heart

21:29.010 --> 21:30.260
Might Aura

21:30.260 --> 21:33.390
Cry out the meaning of your existence

21:33.390 --> 21:34.670
Might Aura

21:34.670 --> 21:38.020
We clash and acknowledge each other's pride

21:38.020 --> 21:47.200
Drawing on what knowledge
and strength as we paint the sky?

21:47.650 --> 21:54.250
Now that we've crossed heaven
and the stars, we'll reveal these emotions

21:54.250 --> 21:58.600
Believe in the next possibility

21:58.600 --> 22:03.380
To return to the roads we believe in

22:03.380 --> 22:07.900
Mighty shine

22:04.470 --> 22:07.900
That light is the brilliant star of our dreams

22:07.900 --> 22:12.390
Mighty wind

22:08.750 --> 22:12.390
That gentle breeze is heaven's wing

22:17.140 --> 22:22.590
We travel as directed by our music

24:05.420 --> 24:07.350
With STARISH's love for you...

24:07.350 --> 24:09.220
With HEAVENS' dreams for you...

24:09.220 --> 24:10.420
Uta Pri!
